# Valgrind suppressions for the JaszczurHAL host test suite.
#
# Referenced by MEMORYCHECK_SUPPRESSIONS_FILE in the root CMakeLists.txt and
# applied automatically by `ctest -T memcheck`.
#
# Keep this list minimal: only suppress allocations that are intentional for
# this project's continuous-operation model (objects that live for the whole
# program lifetime and are deliberately never freed). NEVER add a suppression to
# silence a genuine leak in src/ - fix the code instead.

# ── SmartTimers per-instance lock ────────────────────────────────────────────
# SmartTimers::ensureMutex() lazily allocates one hal_mutex per timer instance
# (create-once, guarded by `if (!_mutex)`). In production a timer is a long-lived
# object, so its lock is held for the program lifetime by design and is never
# destroyed - the project runs continuously and does not tear timers down.
# The host unit tests, however, construct transient SmartTimer instances per
# test case, so Valgrind reports each instance's lock as "definitely lost" when
# the local object goes out of scope. That is a test-harness artifact, not a
# defect, so we suppress this specific allocation site (anchored on
# ensureMutex so nothing else is masked).
{
   SmartTimers-lifetime-bound-mutex-create-once
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:_Znwm
   fun:hal_mutex_create
   fun:_ZN11SmartTimers11ensureMutexEv
   ...
}
